---
import { serializeJsonForHtml } from '../../utils/serialize-json';

interface Props {
  class?: string;
}

const { class: className } = Astro.props;

const demoContent = {
  collections: {
    posts: {
      title: "Posts",
      path: "src/content/posts",
      total: 12,
      entries: [
        {
          id: "script-to-platform",
          title: "From script to platform",
          slug: "script-to-platform",
          status: "published",
          updated: "Today",
          frontmatter: {
            title: "From script to platform",
            slug: "script-to-platform",
            description: "How Chirp becomes part of the Astro development loop.",
            status: "published",
            image: "astro-integration.webp",
            published_at: "2026-08-04",
            category: "Building Chirp",
          },
          markdown: `# From script to platform

Chirp begins as one command inside your Astro project, then progressively reveals the editing surface already described by your schema.

## Native to the development loop

Installed as a development-only Astro integration, Chirp starts with the same command as your site. It reads the same content configuration, edits the same markdown and mdx files, and disappears from the production build.

- One Astro development server
- No second content model
- No editor runtime shipped to production`,
        },
        {
          id: "schema-source",
          title: "Your schema stays the source",
          slug: "schema-as-source",
          status: "draft",
          updated: "2d ago",
          frontmatter: {
            title: "Your schema stays the source",
            slug: "schema-as-source",
            description: "One schema for Astro, Chirp, and every editing surface.",
            status: "draft",
            image: "schema-source.webp",
            published_at: "2026-08-02",
            category: "Architecture",
          },
          markdown: `# Your schema stays the source

Chirp reads the collection definitions your project already trusts. Fields, validation, labels, and editing controls all begin in the same place.

## No duplicate configuration

Change the schema and the editor adapts with it. The content model does not drift away from the site it belongs to.

- Zod defines the structure
- Astro validates the content
- Chirp generates the editing controls`,
        },
        {
          id: "offline-editing",
          title: "Editing without crossing the wire",
          slug: "offline-editing",
          status: "published",
          updated: "5d ago",
          frontmatter: {
            title: "Editing without crossing the wire",
            slug: "offline-editing",
            description: "A local editing loop with no hosted service in the middle.",
            status: "published",
            image: "offline-editing.webp",
            published_at: "2026-07-30",
            category: "Local first",
          },
          markdown: `# Editing without crossing the wire

The integration runs inside the Astro development server. Your drafts, media, and project structure stay local.

## The shortest possible path

An edit moves from the visual canvas to the markdown file in your repository. There is no remote round trip and no production dependency.

- Works with your existing Git workflow
- Keeps unpublished work private
- Remains useful without a connection`,
        },
        {
          id: "better-mdx",
          title: "A better way to work with mdx",
          slug: "better-mdx",
          status: "published",
          updated: "1w ago",
          frontmatter: {
            title: "A better way to work with mdx",
            slug: "better-mdx",
            description: "Visual components without hiding the source beneath them.",
            status: "published",
            image: "better-mdx.webp",
            published_at: "2026-07-27",
            category: "Editing",
          },
          markdown: `# A better way to work with mdx

mdx components appear in the slash menu as purposeful editing surfaces, while the document remains portable source code.

## Visual where it helps

Writers see a useful placeholder and the component properties they can change. Developers keep real Astro components and readable mdx.

- Components are discovered from your configured folder
- Props are exposed in a focused popover
- Imports are handled automatically`,
        },
      ],
    },
    plants: {
      title: "Plants",
      path: "src/content/plants",
      total: 24,
      entries: [
        {
          id: "acai",
          title: "Acai",
          slug: "acai",
          status: "published",
          updated: "Today",
          frontmatter: {
            common_name: "Acai",
            scientific_name: "Euterpe oleracea",
            slug: "acai",
            image: "acai.webp",
            vegetable: false,
            family: "Arecaceae",
            position: "Filtered sun",
          },
          markdown: `# Acai

A slender palm from the Amazon floodplains, best known for its small purple fruit and graceful clustering habit.

## Growing notes

Acai prefers warmth, humidity, and consistently moist soil. Protect young plants from drying winds and strong midday sun.

- Keep evenly watered
- Feed with rich organic matter
- Allow room for multiple stems`,
        },
        {
          id: "banana",
          title: "Banana",
          slug: "banana",
          status: "published",
          updated: "Yesterday",
          frontmatter: {
            common_name: "Banana",
            scientific_name: "Musa",
            slug: "banana",
            image: "banana.webp",
            vegetable: false,
            family: "Musaceae",
            position: "Full sun",
          },
          markdown: `# Banana

Bananas are fast-growing perennial herbs that reward generous feeding, reliable moisture, and protection from wind.

## Growing notes

Maintain one fruiting stem, one follower, and one young sucker in each mat. Mulch heavily and return chopped leaves to the soil.

- Plant in rich, draining soil
- Water deeply in dry weather
- Remove damaged leaves cleanly`,
        },
        {
          id: "cape-gooseberry",
          title: "Cape gooseberry",
          slug: "cape-gooseberry",
          status: "draft",
          updated: "3d ago",
          frontmatter: {
            common_name: "Cape gooseberry",
            scientific_name: "Physalis peruviana",
            slug: "cape-gooseberry",
            image: "cape-gooseberry.webp",
            vegetable: false,
            family: "Solanaceae",
            position: "Full sun",
          },
          markdown: `# Cape gooseberry

A sprawling perennial with lantern-like husks around sweet, tart golden fruit.

## Growing notes

Give the plant space, light support, and a warm position. Fruit is ready when the husk becomes papery and drops naturally.

- Sow after the last cold spell
- Avoid excessive nitrogen
- Harvest fallen fruit frequently`,
        },
        {
          id: "granadilla",
          title: "Granadilla",
          slug: "granadilla",
          status: "published",
          updated: "6d ago",
          frontmatter: {
            common_name: "Granadilla",
            scientific_name: "Passiflora edulis",
            slug: "granadilla",
            image: "granadilla.webp",
            vegetable: false,
            family: "Passifloraceae",
            position: "Sun with cool roots",
          },
          markdown: `# Granadilla

A vigorous evergreen climber producing fragrant flowers and aromatic purple fruit.

## Growing notes

Train the main stem to a strong horizontal support, then allow fruiting laterals to hang down where they remain easy to prune.

- Shelter from strong wind
- Mulch the root zone
- Prune after the main crop`,
        },
      ],
    },
    recipes: {
      title: "Recipes",
      path: "src/content/recipes",
      total: 8,
      entries: [
        {
          id: "charred-brassicas",
          title: "Charred brassicas",
          slug: "charred-brassicas",
          status: "published",
          updated: "Today",
          frontmatter: {
            title: "Charred brassicas",
            slug: "charred-brassicas",
            description: "Wood-fired greens with a bright preserved-lemon dressing.",
            status: "published",
            image: "charred-brassicas.webp",
            serves: 6,
            category: "Shared plates",
          },
          markdown: `# Charred brassicas

Deeply charred seasonal brassicas finished with preserved lemon, toasted seeds, and fresh herbs.

## Method

Cook the vegetables over a fierce fire until the edges blister while the centres remain tender.

- Dress while still warm
- Add herbs at the last moment
- Serve on one generous platter`,
        },
        {
          id: "preserved-lemon-dressing",
          title: "Preserved lemon dressing",
          slug: "preserved-lemon-dressing",
          status: "published",
          updated: "4d ago",
          frontmatter: {
            title: "Preserved lemon dressing",
            slug: "preserved-lemon-dressing",
            description: "A salty, bright dressing for vegetables and grains.",
            status: "published",
            image: "preserved-lemon.webp",
            serves: 8,
            category: "Condiments",
          },
          markdown: `# Preserved lemon dressing

A sharp, savoury dressing that cuts through smoke, olive oil, and rich roasted vegetables.

## Method

Rinse the preserved lemon, remove the seeds, and blend the peel with garlic, vinegar, and olive oil.

- Taste before adding salt
- Loosen with warm water as needed
- Keep refrigerated for one week`,
        },
        {
          id: "tomatillo-salsa",
          title: "Tomatillo salsa",
          slug: "tomatillo-salsa",
          status: "draft",
          updated: "1w ago",
          frontmatter: {
            title: "Tomatillo salsa",
            slug: "tomatillo-salsa",
            description: "A fresh green salsa with fire-roasted tomatillos.",
            status: "draft",
            image: "tomatillo-salsa.webp",
            serves: 4,
            category: "Condiments",
          },
          markdown: `# Tomatillo salsa

Bright, tart tomatillos take on a deeper flavour after a brief char over flame.

## Method

Blacken the tomatillos and chilli, then pulse with onion, coriander, lime, and salt.

- Keep some texture
- Adjust chilli to taste
- Serve the same day`,
        },
        {
          id: "wood-fired-flatbread",
          title: "Wood-fired flatbread",
          slug: "wood-fired-flatbread",
          status: "published",
          updated: "2w ago",
          frontmatter: {
            title: "Wood-fired flatbread",
            slug: "wood-fired-flatbread",
            description: "Soft, blistered flatbread for sharing at the table.",
            status: "published",
            image: "wood-fired-flatbread.webp",
            serves: 8,
            category: "Bread",
          },
          markdown: `# Wood-fired flatbread

A forgiving dough that cooks quickly against the heat of a wood-fired oven or cast-iron plate.

## Method

Stretch each piece by hand, cook until bubbles rise, then turn once and brush with olive oil.

- Rest the dough before shaping
- Keep the work surface lightly floured
- Serve immediately`,
        },
      ],
    },
  },
};

const serialisedDemoContent = serializeJsonForHtml(demoContent);
---

<section
  class:list={["chirp-astro-integration-demo", className]}
  data-chirp-astro-integration
  data-mode="terminal"
  data-browser-screen="entries"
  data-running="false"
  data-complete="false"
  style="visibility: hidden;"
>
  <style is:inline media="not all" data-cai-style>
    [data-chirp-astro-integration],
    [data-chirp-astro-integration] * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] {
      display: block !important;
      width: 100% !important;
      max-width: none !important;
      margin: 0 !important;
      padding: 0 !important;
      border: 0 !important;
      background: transparent !important;
      color: var(--ink, #221e17);
      font-family: var(--mono, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] button,
    [data-chirp-astro-integration] input,
    [data-chirp-astro-integration] [contenteditable] {
      font: inherit;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] button {
      appearance: none;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-frame {
      position: relative;
      width: 100%;
      height: 650px;
      overflow: hidden;
      border: 1px solid var(--dark-line, #453e30);
      border-radius: var(--radius, 14px);
      background: var(--dark, #242019);
      box-shadow: var(--page-shadow, 0 34px 70px -38px #2e261861);
      isolation: isolate;
      transition:
        background 500ms cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1),
        border-color 500ms cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1),
        box-shadow 500ms cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-mode="browser"] .csd-frame {
      border-color: var(--line, #dcd6c3);
      background: var(--surface, #fbf9f2);
      box-shadow: var(--page-shadow, 0 34px 70px -38px #2e261861);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-toolbar {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 10;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      height: 43px;
      padding: 0 15px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--dark-line, #453e30);
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--dark, #242019) 94%, black);
      transition:
        height 420ms cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1),
        padding 420ms cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1),
        border-color 420ms ease,
        background 420ms ease;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-mode="browser"] .csd-toolbar {
      height: 54px;
      padding: 0 13px;
      border-color: var(--line, #dcd6c3);
      background: var(--paper-deep, #fff);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-dots {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 6px;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-dot {
      width: 8px;
      height: 8px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: #5d5542;
      transition: background 420ms ease, transform 420ms ease;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-mode="browser"] .csd-dot:nth-child(1) { background: #d66a4b; }
    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-mode="browser"] .csd-dot:nth-child(2) { background: #d5a94e; }
    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-mode="browser"] .csd-dot:nth-child(3) { background: #7d9a63; }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-terminal-title {
      color: #918977;
      font: 500 10px/1 var(--mono, ui-monospace, monospace) !important;
      transition: opacity 180ms ease, transform 260ms ease;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-mode="browser"] .csd-terminal-title {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateX(-8px);
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-browser-controls {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0 112px 0 63px;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: center;
      gap: 11px;
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(7px);
      pointer-events: none;
      transition: opacity 240ms ease 80ms, transform 360ms cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1) 70ms;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-mode="browser"] .csd-browser-controls {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
      pointer-events: auto;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-nav-buttons {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 4px;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-nav-button {
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      width: 24px;
      height: 24px;
      margin: 0 !important;
      padding: 0 !important;
      border: 0 !important;
      border-radius: 5px !important;
      background: transparent !important;
      color: var(--faint, #6b665a) !important;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-nav-button:hover {
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink, #221e17) 7%, transparent) !important;
      color: var(--ink, #221e17) !important;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-address {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 7px;
      min-width: 0;
      height: 30px;
      padding: 0 11px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line, #dcd6c3);
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface, #fbf9f2) 82%, white);
      color: var(--muted, #59564d);
      font: 500 10px/1 var(--mono, ui-monospace, monospace) !important;
      box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 #ffffffa6;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-lock {
      color: var(--green-text, #47612f);
      font-size: 9px;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-url {
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-replay {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 4;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      margin: 0 0 0 auto !important;
      padding: 4px 0 !important;
      border: 0 !important;
      background: transparent !important;
      color: var(--dark-ok, #a4b88a) !important;
      font: 500 10px/1 var(--mono, ui-monospace, monospace) !important;
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 55%, transparent);
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
      cursor: pointer;
      opacity: 0;
      visibility: hidden;
      transform: translateY(2px);
      transition: opacity 180ms ease, transform 180ms ease, visibility 0s linear 180ms, color 300ms ease;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-complete="true"] .csd-replay {
      opacity: 1;
      visibility: visible;
      transform: translateY(0);
      transition-delay: 90ms, 90ms, 0s, 0s;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-mode="browser"] .csd-replay {
      color: var(--accent-text, #a93619) !important;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-replay:focus-visible,
    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-open-editor:focus-visible,
    [data-chirp-astro-integration] button:focus-visible,
    [data-chirp-astro-integration] [contenteditable]:focus-visible {
      outline: 2px solid var(--accent, #dd4c22);
      outline-offset: 3px;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-stage {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 43px 0 0;
      transition: inset 420ms cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-mode="browser"] .csd-stage {
      inset: 54px 0 0;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-terminal-screen,
    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-browser-screen {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-terminal-screen {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      padding: 29px 32px 26px;
      color: var(--dark-muted, #a49c87);
      font: 500 12px/1.56 var(--mono, ui-monospace, monospace) !important;
      opacity: 1;
      transform: scale(1);
      transform-origin: 50% 45%;
      transition:
        opacity 260ms ease,
        transform 520ms cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1),
        filter 420ms ease;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-mode="browser"] .csd-terminal-screen {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: scale(.965);
      filter: blur(3px);
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-command-line {
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      min-height: 20px;
      color: #e8e1d2;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-prompt,
    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-keyword {
      color: var(--dark-keyword, #e07840);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-command {
      color: #e8e1d2;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-cursor {
      display: inline-block;
      width: .58em;
      height: 1.15em;
      margin-left: 2px;
      vertical-align: -.16em;
      background: var(--accent, #dd4c22);
      animation: csd-cursor 950ms steps(1) infinite;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-running="true"] .csd-cursor,
    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-terminal-ready="true"] .csd-cursor {
      display: none;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-log {
      display: grid;
      gap: 7px;
      width: min(760px, 100%);
      margin-top: 22px;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-task {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.4em minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: baseline;
      min-height: 19px;
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(4px);
      transition: opacity 160ms ease, transform 190ms ease;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-task.is-visible {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-task-icon {
      color: var(--dark-string, #d9a05f);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-task.is-running .csd-task-icon {
      animation: csd-pulse 760ms ease-in-out infinite alternate;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-task.is-complete .csd-task-icon {
      color: var(--dark-ok, #a4b88a);
      animation: none;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-task-label {
      color: #b7ae99;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-task.is-running .csd-task-label {
      color: #e4dccd;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-ready {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.4em minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0;
      width: min(760px, 100%);
      margin-top: 24px;
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(7px);
      transition: opacity 220ms ease, transform 260ms cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-terminal-ready="true"] .csd-ready {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-ready-icon {
      color: var(--dark-ok, #a4b88a);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-ready-copy {
      display: grid;
      gap: 5px;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-ready-title {
      color: #e9e1d2;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-ready-meta {
      color: #817967;
      font-size: 10px;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-astro-status {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 7px;
      width: fit-content;
      margin-top: 3px;
      color: var(--dark-ok, #a4b88a);
      font: 600 10px/1.35 var(--mono, ui-monospace, monospace) !important;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-astro-status::before {
      content: "◆";
      font-size: 7px;
      opacity: .9;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-open-editor {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 7px;
      width: fit-content;
      margin-top: 12px;
      color: var(--dark-string, #d9a05f);
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 60%, transparent);
      text-underline-offset: 4px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-open-editor:hover {
      color: #f0ba78;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-browser-screen {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      min-width: 0;
      min-height: 0;
      color: var(--ink, #221e17);
      font-family: var(--font-system, Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif);
      opacity: 0;
      transform: scale(1.035);
      transform-origin: 50% 45%;
      pointer-events: none;
      transition:
        opacity 360ms ease 120ms,
        transform 560ms cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1) 70ms;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration][data-mode="browser"] .csd-browser-screen {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: scale(1);
      pointer-events: auto;
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-appbar {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 13px;
      height: 48px;
      padding: 0 16px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft, #e5e0cf);
      background: var(--surface, #fbf9f2);
    }

    [data-chirp-astro-integration] .csd-brand {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      color: var(--ink, #221e17);
